      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>With Season 2 around the corner, new stretch goals were announced. One of them was Arena Mode.&nbsp;</p><blockquote><p style=\"color: rgb(2, 6, 33); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; margin: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">How many villains can you defeat in a row with the ultimate hero team? Make your own storyline with this randomized campaign mode and last as long as you can. Fans of the game have made several versions of this idea on the tabletop.</p><p style=\"color: rgb(2, 6, 33); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; margin: 20px 0px 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">If we can reach this goal, Handelabra Games will create an &ldquo;Arena Mode&rdquo; for the video game. The details and options of the new mode will be worked out when we get to the design and development stage, and we&rsquo;ll be getting your input at that time. Some ideas and options include a single fixed hero team with no HP recovery; a drafting mechanic where fallen heroes are replaced; ramping up difficulty with advanced and challenge modes; and more! No matter what, this new mode will keep you on your toes.</p></blockquote><p>Neat idea. I&#39;m largely curious if hero cards will remain in play from one villain to the next, or if everything gets reshuffled. If things remain in play, that could really affect the team you bring; I know having Legacy or Argent Adept all geared up at the start of a match would certainly be a powerful advantage.&nbsp;</p><p>So what features would you want to see in this? And what team would you bring to the arena?</p>",
